🔴 Problems I found:
Problem 1 — No input sanitization on category name
Just like the description field, someone could type <script>alert('x')</script> as a category name. We fixed transactions but forgot categories.
Problem 2 — Category name has no length limit
Someone could type a 500 character category name and break the UI layout completely.
Problem 3 — "Budget Settings" section is empty
There's a card that just says "Manage your monthly allowance..." but does absolutely nothing. It's placeholder text the AI left behind — looks unfinished.
Problem 4 — Case sensitivity issue
Adding "food" and "Food" would create two separate categories since there's no case check.

Fix — Input sanitization ✅
Category names now go through the same sanitizeInput() function we built earlier — no script injection possible.
Fix — 20 character limit ✅
Both the HTML maxlength attribute AND the JavaScript validation enforce this — two layers of protection.
Fix — Case insensitive duplicates ✅
Now "food", "Food" and "FOOD" are all treated as the same category. Uses .toLowerCase() for comparison.
Fix — Empty Budget Settings removed ✅
That placeholder section was just unfinished AI-generated code. Removing it makes the tab look clean and complete.
